Budget: WebSocket fan-out in wsbus must keep p99 publish latency under 5 ms at 500 messages/second sustained. A PR adds durability by fsyncing on every message:

```diff
 func (b *Bus) Publish(topic string, msg []byte) error {
-	b.mu.Lock()
-	defer b.mu.Unlock()
+	b.mu.Lock()
+	defer b.mu.Unlock()
+	if _, err := b.wal.Write(append(msg, '\n')); err != nil {
+		return err
+	}
+	if err := b.wal.Sync(); err != nil {
+		return err
+	}
 	for _, c := range b.subs[topic] {
 		c.send(msg)
 	}
 	return nil
 }
```
The PR description says 'fsync on an SSD is ~0.1 ms so this is fine'. Does this PR meet the budget? Give a verdict, name the specific mechanisms that matter, and specify the measurement you would require before approving.
